\paragraph{Automorphisms and transversal Clifford operations.}

For every $g\in G$, simultaneous translation by $g$ permutes the
qubits within each block through the regular representation
$\mathbb{B}(g)$. Because these translations commute with $A$, $B$,
$C$, and $D$, they preserve the stabilizer group and define
depth-1 code automorphisms. Their induced logical actions are used
in the post-processing of the escaped hypergraph state.

The quadcycle complex also possesses an $X$--$Z$ duality. A transversal Hadamard on all $n$ physical qubits followed by an order-two permutation gives a Hadamard-SWAP, where the permutation swaps the column blocks in the first half of $\mathcal{H}_X/\mathcal{H}_Z$ with those in the second. Writing a logical $Z$ operator by its support on each half as a nontrivial cycle $\mathbb{B}(z_1, z_2) \in \ker \mathcal{H}_X$,
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{B}\begin{pmatrix}
        z_1 \\z_2
    \end{pmatrix} \xmapsto{H\text{-}\mathrm{SWAP}} \mathbb{B}\begin{pmatrix}
        (z_2^*)^T \\
        (z_1^*)^T
    \end{pmatrix} \in \ker \mathcal{H}_Z \setminus \im \mathcal{H}_X^T,
\end{equation}
the map carries low-weight $Z$ operators to low-weight $X$ operators, and therefore $d_X = d_Z$ \cite{bravyi_high-threshold_2024}. The same structure produces a transversal $\overline{CZ}$ gate between two distinct blocks. The duality also yields a fold-transversal $\overline{CZ}$--$\bar S$ gate \cite{breuckmann_fold-transversal_2024}: the $\overline{CZ}$ acts between interchanged pairs of logical qubits, and $\bar S$ on the fixed points of the permutation. Quadcycle codes, like bicycle codes, have no such fixed points, so the $\bar S$ component is absent. Recovering a $\bar S$ gate on bicycle codes requires imposing additional self-dualities~\cite{liang_self-dual_2026}, and we expect similar conditions to result in self-dual quadcycle codes.

\noindent\textbf{Circuit-level noise model}\\ We simulate every tricycle--quadcycle pair in Stim \cite{gidney_stim_2021} under the standard circuit-level depolarizing model (SD6): idling and single-qubit gates are followed by a single-qubit depolarizing channel, two-qubit gates by a two-qubit depolarizing channel, and resets and measurements by a single-qubit flip channel, all at strength $p=10^{-3}$. This is the model used in the cultivation studies we compare against \cite{gidney_magic_2024, sahay2026fold}, so the comparison in \cref{tab:comparison} is made on equal footing. Each physical CCZ triple carries a three-qubit depolarizing channel, in the uniform non-identity-Pauli convention, of strength $p_{\mathrm{CCZ}}=2p$. Because we simulate only a single tricycle--quadcycle pair, the other two legs of every triple belong to the remaining factory copies and are traced out. Since the transversal $\overline{\mathrm{CCZ}}$ is depth one, each simulated qubit takes part in exactly one triple, so the reduced channel is exactly the single-qubit marginal of the three-qubit channel, namely depolarizing noise of strength $\tfrac{16}{21}\,p_{\mathrm{CCZ}} = \tfrac{32}{21}\,p$. Tracing out the other legs erases cross-block correlations in the CCZ channel, which we expect to make both the logical error rate and the acceptance fraction conservative. Acceptance fractions are reported per block. The full factory requires all three pairs to be accepted, so its yield is the cube of the quoted value, which is what enters the space-time volumes of \cref{tab:comparison}.

