\noindent\textbf{A four-dimensional receiving code}\\ Three complementary features make the factory efficient. First, both code families are single-shot in the relevant bases, which keeps the protocol shallow. This generates the magic states rapidly and, just as importantly, confines postselection to a small space-time volume, making full error detection practical. Second, the dimension jump ends with a transversal measurement of the tricycle block, which exposes the full redundancy of the code and is effectively immune to measurement errors. In a generic mid-circuit postselection step, transversally measuring the data would collapse the computational state. Here the measurement is already the teleportation primitive that transfers the logical information into a separate quadcycle block, so its outcomes can be used for strong postselection without disturbing the escaped magic state.

